VDR image_next — native image viewer and slideshow
=================================================

This fork builds on the VDR Image plugin and its 2022 FFmpeg updates.
The native decoder uses libavcodec/libswscale rather than the historical
imageplugin.sh conversion scripts. The current development version is
read from the root VERSION file (currently 0.7.0-rc1; see HISTORY).
The Makefile passes this version to the compiled VDR plugin as
IMAGE_PLUGIN_VERSION. Do not edit version strings independently in C++ sources.

Requirements
------------
- VDR development headers and pkg-config (tested compilation with VDR 2.8.x
  still needs to be verified on the target distribution)
- FFmpeg development libraries: libavcodec, libavformat, libswscale
- Optional: libexif for metadata and fast JPEG thumbnail extraction
- Optional: libskindesignerapi development package for Skindesigner mode

Build using the usual VDR plugin make targets. Set WITH_SKINDESIGNER=0
to build without the Skindesigner API, even when it is installed.

Configuring sources
-------------------
Place imagesources.conf in the image_next plugin configuration directory.
Legacy entries from the image plugin configuration directory are also read.

Syntax: path;display name;needs mount (0/1);filename patterns
Example:
  /srv/photos;Photos;0;*.jpg *.jpeg *.png *.tif* *.bmp

A missing or empty imagesources.conf will not expose the filesystem root.
The menu instead displays "No image sources configured".

SuiteOSD image gallery (native VDR services)
------------------------------------------
The SuiteOSD plugin can request configured photo sources, browse folders,
receive thumbnails from image_next's existing asynchronous cache and launch
a selected photo/slideshow through the existing image_next player. No second
decoder, player or HTTP API is added. Every relative path is validated
against an imagesources.conf root after resolving symlinks.

The versioned C++ VDR plugin service ABI is documented in
docs/suiteosd-service.md and image-next-service-v1.h. Both plugins must
be built against the same VDR ABI. SuiteOSD's initial gallery is
implemented on its main development branch (0.9.3-dev). Actual VDR
remote-control and TV output acceptance is still required.

Picture output
--------------
The plugin setup now offers three picture output modes:
  Automatic (OSD / MPEG-2) — default. Uses true-color OSD if supported,
                             otherwise the traditional MPEG-2 device output.
  True-color OSD            — requests direct OSD first, with MPEG-2 fallback
                             if the device cannot provide the requested area.
  Legacy MPEG-2             — always uses the previous video-output path.

This setting applies to full-screen images, slideshow, zoom and jump preview.
The standard VDR remote-control keys remain unchanged. JPEG/PNG/other images
are decoded by FFmpeg on the image worker thread, and only a ready ARGB frame
is transferred to the foreground thread for the VDR cOsd::DrawImage call.
A 32-bpp true-color OSD covering the current OSD resolution is required;
this is a VDR output-device feature, not a VAAPI-only API.

Existing UseDeviceStillPicture and LiveAudio settings are preserved. The
former controls only the legacy MPEG-2 output mode.

Display modes
-------------
In the image_next plugin setup:
  0: List
  1: Grid (C++)      -- works with the native VDR OSD, without Skindesigner
  2: Grid (Skin XML) -- needs a compatible active Skindesigner skin

IMPORTANT: Building against Skindesigner is not enough! The active XML skin
must provide the template named plug-image_next-grid.xml. A reference
template is included in skindesigner/plug-image_next-grid.xml.
The build records the actual libskindesignerapi version from pkg-config.
Install a copy into the xmlfiles/ directory of your ACTIVE Skindesigner skin,
then reload the skin or restart VDR as required by Skindesigner.
For example, the target filename is:
  <skindesigner skin root>/<active-skin>/xmlfiles/plug-image_next-grid.xml

The active skin's location is configured by the Skindesigner plugin. Do not
assume a fixed yaVDR, MLD, or Debian path.

This file matches the following C++ registrations:
  plugin name   image_next
  root view     grid
  view elements background / header
  view grid     imagegrid
  tokens        thumbnail, albumname, is_folder, current

If the current skin is not a Skindesigner skin or it does not expose the
plugin view, mode 2 falls back to the native C++ grid and logs the reason.
If a template fails to parse or initialize, inspect the VDR logs for
"skindesigner" and "imageplugin" errors before changing the skin.

Files and thumbnails
--------------------
Pictures remain in their original directories. If present, folder.jpg is
used as a directory cover. Photo directories are NOT modified just because
a directory is opened: the old automatic EXIF-to-folder.jpg writer has
been removed. JPEG EXIF thumbnails for the native grid are extracted into
a unique temporary file and deleted after use.

The asynchronous native grid loads only visible tiles and uses an LRU bitmap
cache with a 64 MiB budget (up to 100 cached thumbnails). Cache entries
include image file size and modification time to avoid serving outdated
thumbnails when a file changes. EXIF orientation, including mirrored camera
orientations, is applied to thumbnails and to full-size/zoomed playback.
The new player prefers full-screen true-color VDR OSD output without
MPEG-2 recompression. The original MPEG-2 still-image path remains available
as a compatibility fallback for output plugins without a suitable 32-bpp OSD.

The existing imagecmds.conf functionality can run explicitly configured
commands; only enable commands you trust.

Quick manual smoke test
-----------------------
1. Configure a valid imagesources.conf with a small JPEG photo directory.
2. Build with Skindesigner support; ensure a Skindesigner skin is active.
3. Select mode 1 and verify the native grid, arrows, OK, Back and slideshow.
4. Copy the XML file into the active skin's xmlfiles/ and reload Skindesigner.
5. Select mode 2; verify grid visibility, highlighted selection and images.
6. Switch to a non-Skindesigner skin: mode 2 must fall back to the C++ grid.
7. Remove/rename imagesources.conf: verify the informative menu, not root /.
8. Verify no folder.jpg is generated in photo directories.

Source-only checks (no VDR installation necessary)
--------------------------------------------------
  python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v

These checks verify the C++/XML naming contract, normalized grid geometry,
fallback presence, optional dependencies and cache/EXIF invariants. They
are not a substitute for compiling against VDR and Skindesigner, nor for
visual tests using the active Skindesigner skin. This development branch
has not been installed on the user's VDR.

Known limitations
-----------------
OSD picture rendering has no independent hardware test yet. Actual RGB
resolution depends on the device's advertised VDR OSD size; high-resolution
photo quality cannot exceed the available OSD resolution. The legacy MPEG-2
fallback remains present and unchanged for devices without true-color OSD.
This is not a specialized VAAPI texture renderer (no VAAPI requirement).
A JPEG embedded EXIF thumbnail can still be used for fast grid loading.

On an actual VDR, verify fullscreen, slideshow, zoom, jump, image commands,
native grid, Skindesigner grid and each Picture output setting before
merging the draft pull request.

